@startuml dfd_level_0
' ==========================================================
' Actors / External Entities
' ==========================================================
actor User

' ==========================================================
' External Data Stores
' ==========================================================
folder "Raw Input (CSV / Directory)" as INPUT
database "Master HDF5 Bundle\n(.h5)\n(version 2.0, major/minor/patch attrs)" as MASTER
folder "Protocol PDF / Info" as PROTOINFO
folder "Raw ZIP Bundle (optional)" as RAWZIP
folder "Exported Protocol Files\n(.npz, .dsr.npz, …)" as EXPORT

' ==========================================================
' Processes
' ==========================================================
rectangle "convert_any_to_hdf5\n(main)" as CONV_IN
rectangle "convert_hdf5_to_format\n(main)" as CONV_OUT

' ==========================================================
' Data Flows
' ==========================================================
User --> CONV_IN : invoke CLI\n(-i, -o, --protocol …)
CONV_IN --> INPUT    : reads raw data
CONV_IN --> PROTOINFO: reads protocol PDF (optional)
CONV_IN --> RAWZIP   : creates zipped raw bundle (optional)

' New output hierarchy inside the master bundle:
'   /StandardFormat/Output/Map  (contains populations → neurons → times/voltage)
CONV_IN --> MASTER   : writes MasterBundle (incl. Output/Map, version attrs)

User --> CONV_OUT  : invoke CLI\n(-i, -o, protocol sub‑command …)
CONV_OUT --> MASTER   : reads MasterBundle
CONV_OUT --> PROTOINFO: may need protocol PDF (validation / metadata)
CONV_OUT --> EXPORT   : writes protocol‑specific files (.npz, …)

' ==========================================================
' Notes
' ==========================================================
note right of MASTER
  • Root attribute: format_version (legacy string)
  • New integer attrs: format_version_major, format_version_minor,
    format_version_patch
  • Global section now stores a mapping of standard metadata keys
  • Output group renamed from “OutputSpikes” → “Output/Map”
  • Protocol group stores:
      – “Version” attribute (UTF‑8 string)
      – Compressed “Content” dataset (uint8 PDF bytes)
end note

@enduml